### Theo — no longer in Acme — founds a company of his own, and is its dispatcher
# @name TheoCreatesGarage
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{TheoAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Theo's Garage" }

### A self-made dispatcher is a dispatcher in his tenant, not of the project: `regions.create` names `admin` only
# @name TheoWritesRegions
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{TheoAccess}}
X-Alvo-Tenant: {{TheoCreatesGarage.response.body.$.tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{RegionCode}}T", "name": "Theo's region" }

### Dana, Acme's founder, is no different (plan D2)
# @name DanaWritesRegions
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaAccess}}
X-Alvo-Tenant: {{AcmeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{RegionCode}}D", "name": "Dana's region" }

### Theo invites Dana into his garage — as a technician
# @name TheoInvitesDana
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/tenants/{{TheoCreatesGarage.response.body.$.tenantId}}/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{TheoAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roles": ["technician"] }

###
# @name DanaAccepts
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/invitations/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{TheoInvitesDana.response.body.$.code}}" }

### In the garage, Dana is a technician: `customers.create` names dispatcher and admin
# @name DanaCreatesInGarage
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaAccess}}
X-Alvo-Tenant: {{TheoCreatesGarage.response.body.$.tenantId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{TheoCreatesGarage.response.body.$.tenantId}}",
  "name": "A garage customer",
  "tier": "standard"
}

### The same person, the same body, in Acme: a dispatcher there. Two tenants, two role sets.
# @name DanaCreatesInAcme
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaAccess}}
X-Alvo-Tenant: {{AcmeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{AcmeId}}",
  "name": "A garage customer",
  "tier": "standard"
}

### The control for both region refusals: the one role `regions.create` names may write it
# @name AdminCreatesRegion2
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/regions
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{RegionCode}}2", "name": "Self-service region two" }
